<title>SWEDEN: Market not ready to up pulp price before Q4 - SCA.</title>
<headline>Market not ready to up pulp price before Q4 - SCA.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish forestry group SCA said on Friday that the market would not be ready for pulp price increases before the fourth quarter of 1997.  </p>
<p>&quot;To raise just before the summer period seems unrealistic,&quot; SCA's managing director Sverker Martin-Lof told Reuters via his secretary Ingrid Deljemark.</p>
<p>&quot;A better time would be the fourth quarter this year.&quot;</p>
<p>He said buyers had already stocked up on the pulp that they needed for the holiday period.</p>
<p>&quot;According to my estimates all the buyers have already stocked up with pulp for over the holiday,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>&quot;The market will not be ready for any price increases before the fourth quarter.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
